​{
  "id": 27,
  "name": "CellTiter-Glo 2.0 Cell Viability Assay",
  "group": "Copilot",
  "notes": "Automated executable template for the CellTiter-Glo 2.0 viability workflow on Nigel_System. Manual_setup reagent thaw, room-temperature equilibration, and gentle inversion steps were intentionally excluded from executable threads and must be completed off-system before automation begins. CellTiter-Glo 2.0 reagent is assumed to be staged into a protected dispenser-compatible reservoir/presentation before the dispense step. Compound dosing is implemented as Prime LiquidTransfer with a dedicated tips thread because the transfer is contamination-critical and dispenses into wells already containing cells/media. Prime LiquidTransfer parameter specs and discrete deck nest resources were not provided in workflow state; tray/PrimeStore placeholders are used for resource binding and Prime method/deck details require engineering completion before validation. The treated-cell incubation duration/conditions remain user-defined and may require off-system 37C/CO2 incubation. Ambient assay-plate equilibration and post-lysis stabilization are encoded with Incubate steps plus pauseAfter delays of 1800s and 600s, respectively.",
